1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,222
An earthquake lasts seconds.

2
00:00:02,222 --> 00:00:04,889
The cost stays with you.

3
00:00:04,889 --> 00:00:10,667
Think of a small shop in Colombia: a cracked window, lost
stock.

4
00:00:10,667 --> 00:00:16,000
A loss below the deductible can still overwhelm a family's
savings.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,042
I built Aivy Quorum for parametric cover: agree the trigger

6
00:00:21,042 --> 00:00:23,333
and payout in advance.

7
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:27,000
Verify the earthquake, not every broken window.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,889
Let's try Medellín.

9
00:00:28,889 --> 00:00:32,194
Pick a place and a budget.

10
00:00:32,194 --> 00:00:37,861
Drag through history to compare premiums for the same eight-
hundred-dollar payout.

11
00:00:37,861 --> 00:00:40,222
This is a model.

12
00:00:40,222 --> 00:00:44,000
Payment depends on the agreed earthquake conditions.

13
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,089
Here, I pay with funded test tokens.

14
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:50,133
No wallet extension.

15
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:55,756
This creates a real cover NFT, publishes the terms, and

16
00:00:55,756 --> 00:00:58,822
schedules the payout on Hedera.

17
00:00:58,822 --> 00:01:00,867
Here's the receipt.

18
00:01:00,867 --> 00:01:07,000
The tokens have no cash value, but these transactions really
happened.

19
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,500
The agent pays three oracle services through Blocky402 using
x402.

20
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:15,500
Each checks the recorded conditions.

21
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:18,000
Here are the receipts.

22
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,500
No matching earthquake was found, so the payout stays
locked.

23
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,000
Buying data is not buying approval.

24
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,880
This is why Hedera matters.

25
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:34,200
The agent signs the exact transfer in advance.

26
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:38,520
Two of three oracle keys must also sign.

27
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:43,320
Then Hedera executes it, without a separate executor
transaction.

28
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:47,160
This recorded mainnet experiment moved four HBAR.

29
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:50,1000
Controlled signatures, not a real earthquake claim.

30
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,762
The workflow has spending limits and saved transaction IDs.

31
00:01:55,762 --> 00:02:01,000
Even all three oracle keys cannot spend without the agent.

32
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:07,029
My npm-published Uniswap plugin lets Hedera Agent Kit
developers access EVM liquidity.

33
00:02:07,029 --> 00:02:12,130
Here, Quorum adds guarded execution: my Axelar plugin builds
the

34
00:02:12,130 --> 00:02:16,768
bridge, and Uniswap's Trading API prepares the Sepolia swap.

35
00:02:16,768 --> 00:02:21,870
These demo-account tokens are separate from the locked cover
reserve.

36
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:24,652
Review, confirm, inspect the receipts.

37
00:02:24,652 --> 00:02:29,754
Funded test wallets make it easy to try, without a

38
00:02:29,754 --> 00:02:33,000
wallet extension or custom swap contract.

39
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:38,280
Uniswap has a real position NFT, fee collection, and
withdrawal.

40
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:40,200
That's trading liquidity.

41
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:45,000
Earthquake-cover deposits go into a separate, shared Hedera
pool.

42
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,897
Twenty-five test tokens buy twenty-five ARPS.

43
00:02:47,897 --> 00:02:50,793
ARPS earnings and exits aren't enabled.

44
00:02:50,793 --> 00:02:52,448
Brokers earn commissions.

45
00:02:52,448 --> 00:02:57,000
Future revenue could come from service fees for insurance
partners.

46
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,176
Here's the part I'd want for myself: less to remember.

47
00:03:02,176 --> 00:03:07,353
On Aivy Labs, I set a monthly budget for Medellín.

48
00:03:07,353 --> 00:03:12,529
Ten test tokens, at least eight hundred in conditional
cover.

49
00:03:12,529 --> 00:03:15,353
My first policy is issued.

50
00:03:15,353 --> 00:03:21,000
I can ask, 'Am I covered?' And pause future purchases
anytime.

51
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,897
Quorum answers that question too.

52
00:03:23,897 --> 00:03:29,207
It reads Hedera through Mirror Node and links the evidence.

53
00:03:29,207 --> 00:03:35,000
The AI explains; it cannot sign, spend, or change my policy.

54
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:40,176
Earlier Aivy, my published Uniswap and Axelar plugins, and
Mirror

55
00:03:40,176 --> 00:03:42,529
Node skill are reused.

56
00:03:42,529 --> 00:03:47,706
New here: quote-only Uniswap tooling, a reusable settlement
plugin, guarded

57
00:03:47,706 --> 00:03:51,000
cover, paid oracles, and monthly agents.

58
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,889
The goal is simple: less uncertainty when people need help.

59
00:03:55,889 --> 00:03:59,000
A promise you can actually verify.
